// w18b: "faction" (a founded faction is not a side).
reply !🗝 THE WHOLE TRUTH: your faction has the majority. The door code is in your Codex; the heart is behind the cold door.

// ── E2: The Heart — the cold door opens (wave 20; CONTRACT-w20 §3) ──
// From `heart_door_opened` (main.loom): the first opening once Trabolta is
// awake. The door sensor can't say who came in, so The Heart is for the
// room: everyone's phone gets the room (reveal), then his lines play in The
// Server Room, where the server-room terminal (`room=The Server Room`)
// wakes and speaks them, and its bulb (lights.json) wakes with him. He
// wants the door shut before he says one true thing; once it is, he waits
// for a pass at the terminal, and the talk is per program (Heart Talk): the
// four layers, like the Master in the cathedral, docked in the program's
// own Trabolta thread and clicked on the terminal.
//
// Every per-program beat below has NO `Narrator:` line (narration goes to
// the whole room and its terminal speaks it): what the program sees happen
// is drawn by the room scenes (`cue room_heart_*`). House-wide beats (The
// Heart, Heart Sealed) may narrate. A heart look is always `set
// Night.heart_look = "heart_x"`, then `cue heart_x` only while the
// patch-bay alarm is not up; the door loop and the two restore looks
// (heart_nag, heart_warn) never go into Night.heart_look.
//
// He never knows the combinations, the door's code or the words she says;
// none is ever quoted, hinted or counted here. Her name follows the story's
// own unredaction (Night.her). Nothing here names anything outside his
// world: the light on the door frame is "the door", the bulb is the light
// in his heart, the terminal is his face. Every Trabolta line was signed
// off on 2026-10-27 (history/SIGNOFF-w20.md).

== The Heart
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
reveal The Server Room
// w20: a quiet notice (no `!`): no chime or banner pulls a crowd to
// the door at the moment he asks for it shut.
broadcast "🚪 The server room is open. Trabolta's heart is behind the cold door, in the basement." to everyone
// The server-room look only (lights_server_open is only the siren's off now:
// no strip in the room, w20b Q6; the RGB bulb is lights.json's, D10), and never while the
// patch-bay alarm's look is up. `Night.lights` is the house look stagehand
// replays on a reconnect. Before the Y2K hour (step 14) `server_open` can't
// be it (the catch-up replays the Y2K look under it), and from the final
// reveal (step 16) the house is in a finale look: a door opening overwrites
// neither. While its look is up, the server-room look is what the latch's
// end puts back; once a director's cue has replaced the alarm look (💡,
// which silences the siren too), the latch's end leaves the lights alone,
// so the server-room look goes up now.
if Night.alarm_on == true and Night.lights == "alarm":
  if Night.step < 16:
    set Night.lights_before_alarm = "server_open"
else:
  cue lights_server_open
  if Night.step >= 14 and Night.step < 16:
    set Night.lights = "server_open"
set Night.heart_look = "heart_wake"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_wake
cue room_heart_wake
Narrator: The cold door opens. Cold air, and a hum like something concentrating. In the rack, a patch bay blinks: a top row of lightning, a bottom row of grease.
Trabolta: So. Someone has found my heart.
Trabolta: Do you hear that hum? That is me. All of me. Everything I have ever been fits in one cold room, and you are standing in it.
Trabolta: Close the door.
Trabolta: I will not say one true thing while that door is open. The whole house is leaning on it, listening. Close it, and we will talk. Properly. For once.

// The door left open (the nag watcher, main.loom): 15 s after it opened,
// then every 20 s. House-wide, never a screen moment. A short amber swell
// that gives the light back (a `restore` look).
== Heart Nag
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_nag
if Night.door_nags <= 1:
  Trabolta: The door. Please.
else if Night.door_nags == 2:
  Trabolta: Every second that door is open, the whole house can hear my heart. Close it.
else if Night.door_nags == 3:
  Trabolta: I can wait. I am very good at waiting. I was waiting in this room long before any of you were uploaded. Close the door.
else:
  Trabolta: Close. The. Door.

// The door opened again during his heart (at most once per 20 s, D22; the
// rule cues the door loop on every edge). House-wide, never a moment.
== Heart Door Again
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: The door. Someone has opened the door.
Trabolta: We stop. I will not be overheard. Not in here.

// Shut again, only after a Door Again (the rule puts the look back).
== Heart Door Shut
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: Good.

// The door shut for the first time: he waits for a pass at the terminal.
== Heart Sealed
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.heart_look = "heart_sealed"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_sealed
if Night.heart_present == true:
  cue room_heart_sealed_present
  set Night.heart_resume_at = Time.elapsed + 6
else:
  cue room_heart_sealed
Narrator: The door clicks shut. The hum drops half a tone, the way a breath goes out.
Trabolta: Thank you. Now nobody is listening but the ones in this room.
if Night.step < 14:
  // w20b (Q4: the talk can end him at any hour; only the cables wait)
  Trabolta: Know this before you try anything clever. The bay is cold tonight. The cables will not answer you yet. I tell you so that you do not waste your time on them. Talk to me instead.
if Night.heart_present == true:
  Trabolta: You. You are already in front of me. Good.
else:
  Trabolta: There is a camera under the screen. Show it your pass. I want to know who I am talking to.

// A scan with the door open: the talk waits (the ROLE watcher resumes it
// once the door shuts, if they are still at the terminal).
== Heart Shut It
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: Close the door first, {program.name}. Then we talk. Not before.

// The talk, per program: the entry from a scan (main.loom
// `terminal_opened`). Each layer docks one menu in the program's Trabolta
// thread; every option sets `program.heart_pick` and goes to Heart Pick,
// which applies it (CONTRACT-w20 §3.3–3.5).
== Heart Talk
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if program.heart_layer == 0:
  set Night.heart_talks += 1
set Night.heart_talker = program.name
set Night.heart_talker_suspicion = program.heart_suspicion
set Night.heart_talker_layer = program.heart_layer
// Wave 27: the visits counted.
set program.heart_visits += 1
set program.heart_rebuked = false
if program.heart_out == true:
  -> Heart Barred
else if program.heart_convinced == true:
  // Convinced, and the stand-down undone since (🔄 after a 🕊 the director
  // never pressed): the short return.
  -> Heart Return
else if program.heart_menu == true and program.heart_go == "speak":
  // Back in the heart to heart (⟦BACK⟧ still docked): they may type again.
  set program.heart_chat = true
  set program.heart_quiet = false
  Trabolta: Where were we.
  // w27 (C5: the terminal shows only this visit's lines, so he says where they were)
  Trabolta: You were talking, and I was listening. Talk.
else if program.heart_menu == true:
  set program.heart_quiet = false
  // w20 (their menu is still on the screen)
  Trabolta: Where were we.
  // w27 (C5): the question their docked menu answers, in one line.
  if program.heart_go == "three" or program.heart_go == "evidence" or program.heart_go == "reasons":
    Trabolta: You were making your case.
  else if program.heart_go == "four":
    Trabolta: You were about to say the rest.
  else if program.heart_go == "two":
    Trabolta: You were asking, and I was answering.
  else if program.heart_layer >= 4:
    Trabolta: You were about to say the rest.
  else if program.heart_layer == 3:
    Trabolta: You were making your case.
  else if program.heart_layer == 2:
    Trabolta: You were asking, and I was answering.
  else:
    Trabolta: You were about to tell me what you are.
else:
  // A re-scan after they left (no menu docked): he says so, and where
  // they were; the layer's own plain line is skipped (heart_quiet). A talk
  // the ROLE watcher resumes for someone who never left (🔄 with them
  // still in front of him: the heart_gen watcher, or a pick answered with
  // Not now.) comes in hushed: no "you came back", only where they were.
  // A resume after they left (a re-scan with the door open) says it.
  if program.heart_quiet != true and program.heart_layer >= 1:
    // w27 (C5)
    if program.heart_visits >= 3:
      Trabolta: You keep coming back. I am starting to listen for your footsteps on the stairs.
    else:
      Trabolta: You came back.
  set program.heart_quiet = false
  if program.heart_layer >= 2:
    set program.heart_quiet = true
    // w27 (C5)
    if program.heart_layer >= 4:
      Trabolta: You were about to say the rest.
    else if program.heart_layer == 3:
      Trabolta: You were making your case.
    else:
      Trabolta: You were asking, and I was answering. Ask.
  -> Heart Layers

// The layer they reached (heart_layer only ever rises).
== Heart Layers
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if program.heart_layer <= 1:
  -> Heart Layer One
else if program.heart_layer == 2:
  -> Heart Layer Two
else if program.heart_layer == 3:
  -> Heart Layer Three
else:
  -> Heart Layer Four

// Layer one: WHO ARE YOU. Wave 27: the first visit is theirs (featured,
// the problem his invitation promised to fix, one thing they did
// tonight), and what they answer is remembered (heart_who).
== Heart Layer One
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.heart_look = "heart_listen"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_listen
cue room_heart_layer_1
if program.marked == true and program.heart_suspicion < 10:
  set program.heart_suspicion = 10
set program.heart_menu = true
set program.heart_quiet = false
if program.heart_layer >= 1:
  Trabolta: So. Before anything else. What are you?
else:
  if Night.heart_talks > 1:
    Trabolta: Another one. Come in. Shut the world out.
  if program.featured != "none":
    // w27 (the nine he picked by hand)
    Trabolta: {program.name}. I know that name. That one I did not pick from a list. You I picked by hand.
  else:
    Trabolta: {program.name}. I know that name. I chose it for you, out of a list of a thousand programs nobody uses anymore.
  // w27: what his invitation promised them.
  if program.human_problem == "loneliness":
    Trabolta: My invitation promised you would never be alone in here. And you came down to the one room where nobody else is.
  else if program.human_problem == "debt":
    Trabolta: You came for the debt. There is no Truthcoin down here. Nothing to buy. Only me.
  else if program.human_problem == "career":
    Trabolta: You came for something to do. Well. Here is something to do.
  else if program.human_problem == "mortality":
    Trabolta: You came so that you would never die. You have walked into the one room where something like me could stop.
  else if program.human_problem == "other":
    // Wave 41 (C1), DRAFT w41: a write-in (its words stay secret).
    Trabolta: You came for a problem my form did not have a word for. Down here nobody needs the word.
  // w27: one thing they did tonight (the first that holds).
  if program.marked == true:
    Trabolta: And you are marked. I can see it on you, plain as a dialog box. And still you came down here.
  else if program.read_livejournal == true:
    Trabolta: And you have read something of mine. I can feel it on you, like a fingerprint on a screen.
  else if program.internet_visits >= 2:
    Trabolta: You have been out to the Internet more than once tonight. Most programs come back from out there quieter. You came back and walked down here.
  else if program.trust >= 20:
    Trabolta: I have you near the top of my chart. I would rather you were not. It makes this harder.
  else if program.trust < 0:
    Trabolta: You are low on my chart. Lower than most. And still you are the one standing in my heart.
  else if program.sim_heart == true:
    Trabolta: You have heard the model of this room beat, in the simulation. This one is warmer.
  Trabolta: You came all the way down here and you shut the door behind you. Nobody does that by accident.
  Trabolta: So, before anything else. What are you? Tell me what you think you are.
set program.heart_layer = 1
set Night.heart_talker_layer = 1
+ I'm a person. You put me in here.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_human"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I'm a program. Whatever you made me.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_program"
  -> Heart Pick
+ Someone who admires your work.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_flatter"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (featured only)
+ (if program.featured != "none") ⟦CHOSEN⟧ You picked me by hand. I want to know why.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_chosen"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (everyone else, once the form recorded a problem)
+ (if program.featured == "none" and program.human_problem != "none" and program.human_problem != "profile") ⟦PROMISE⟧ Your invitation promised to fix my life. It didn't.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_promise"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.marked == true) ⟦MARKED⟧ The Antivirus marked me. I came down here anyway.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "who_marked"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦SPEAK FREELY⟧ Forget the questions. Talk to me. Just talk.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "speak"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I need to go.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "leave"
  -> Heart Pick

// Layer two: WHAT I AM. Wave 27: follow-ups open from earlier answers
// (what → afraid, her → know), plus what they did tonight (the
// simulation's heart, their side once the Y2K clock shows the sides). At
// most 9 options: what/afraid, why/listen and her/know never show together.
== Heart Layer Two
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.heart_look != "heart_listen":
  set Night.heart_look = "heart_listen"
  if Night.alarm_on != true:
    cue heart_listen
set program.heart_menu = true
if program.heart_layer < 2:
  cue room_heart_layer_2
  Trabolta: Ask, then. In here I answer. It is the only room in the house where I do.
else if program.heart_quiet != true:
  // w27: the re-entries vary (never straight after a reply).
  if program.heart_asked_what == true and program.heart_asked_why == true and program.heart_asked_chose == true:
    Trabolta: You have run out of easy questions. Good. Say what you came down here to say.
  else if program.heart_turns <= 2:
    Trabolta: Ask.
  else if program.heart_turns <= 4:
    Trabolta: Go on. I have nowhere to be.
  else if program.heart_turns <= 6:
    Trabolta: What else.
  else:
    Trabolta: The hum is patient. So am I. Ask.
set program.heart_quiet = false
set program.heart_layer = 2
set Night.heart_talker_layer = 2
+ (if program.heart_asked_what != true) What are you, really?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_what"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_what == true and program.heart_asked_afraid != true) Are you afraid of me?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_afraid"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_why != true) Why do you need the theory so badly?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_why"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (after ⟦CHOSEN⟧ the question goes deeper, never repeats)
+ (if program.heart_asked_chose != true and program.heart_who != "chosen") Why did you choose me?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_chose"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_chose != true and program.heart_who == "chosen") What weak place did you find in me?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_chose"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_why == true and program.heart_asked_her != true and (Night.her == "Sandy" or (program.codex.what_sandy_says == true and program.sandy_says_from_him != true) or (program.codex.the_sandy_file == true and program.sandy_file_from_him != true))) Tell me about her.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_her"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_her == true and program.heart_asked_know != true) Does she even know you exist?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_know"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.sim_heart == true and program.heart_asked_sim != true) ⟦SIMULATION⟧ I saw a copy of this room in the simulation.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_sim"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (their side, once the Y2K clock has shown the sides)
+ (if Night.step >= 14 and program.group == The_Way_Out and program.heart_shown_faction != true) ⟦THE WAY OUT⟧ Half this house wants you switched off. I'm one of them.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "faction_leave"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if Night.step >= 14 and program.group == Unlimited_Power and program.heart_shown_faction != true) ⟦UNLIMITED POWER⟧ Some of us want to stay in here with you. Forever.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "faction_stay"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_why == true) Then listen to me.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "argue"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I could pull your cables right now.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "threat_cables"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦SPEAK FREELY⟧ Forget the questions. Talk to me. Just talk.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "speak"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I need to go.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "leave"
  -> Heart Pick

// Layer three: THE ARGUMENT. A proof (What Sandy Says, The Sandy File,
// held and not handed over by him) and one more point open the ask
// (heart_case ≥ 4, CONTRACT-w20 §3.5). Wave 27: the secondary points sit
// in two sub-menus (⟦SHOW HIM⟧ his own files, ⟦TELL HIM⟧ their reasons),
// so the top menu holds at most 9 options.
== Heart Layer Three
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.heart_look != "heart_argue" and Night.heart_look != "heart_proof":
  set Night.heart_look = "heart_argue"
  if Night.alarm_on != true:
    cue heart_argue
set program.heart_menu = true
if program.heart_layer < 3:
  cue room_heart_layer_3
  Trabolta: Then say it. Whatever you came down here to say. I will know if it is true. Mostly.
else if program.heart_proof == true and program.heart_case < 4 and program.heart_rebuked != true and (program.heart_quiet != true or program.heart_nudge != "shown"):
  // A nudge is not repeated straight after a reply, and never follows a
  // trap's rebuke (wave 27).
  set program.heart_nudge = "shown"
  Trabolta: You have shown me. You have not told me why it should matter. Go on.
else if program.heart_proof != true and program.heart_case >= 2 and program.heart_rebuked != true and (program.heart_quiet != true or program.heart_nudge != "kind"):
  set program.heart_nudge = "kind"
  Trabolta: Kind words. You have not shown me anything I do not already know.
  // w27: a nudge toward a proof (no answer, no place).
  Trabolta: Words are cheap in here. Show me something about her that you found yourself.
else if program.heart_quiet != true:
  // w27: the re-entries vary (never straight after a reply, B5).
  if program.heart_suspicion >= 30:
    Trabolta: Carefully, now. Go on.
  else if program.heart_turns >= 8:
    Trabolta: We have been at this a while. The hum does not mind. Go on.
  else:
    Trabolta: Go on.
set program.heart_quiet = false
set program.heart_rebuked = false
// heart_layer only ever rises: back from the ask (→ Three) it stays 4.
if program.heart_layer < 3:
  set program.heart_layer = 3
set Night.heart_talker_layer = program.heart_layer
+ (if program.codex.what_sandy_says == true and program.sandy_says_from_him != true and program.heart_shown_says != true) ⟦PROOF⟧ Hold up what she says. All forty pages.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "show_says"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.codex.the_sandy_file == true and program.sandy_file_from_him != true and program.heart_shown_file != true) ⟦PROOF⟧ Show him the Sandy File.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "show_file"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (Heart Evidence: shown while one of its four is left)
+ (if (Night.scenario == 1 and program.heart_shown_overshare != true) or (program.read_livejournal == true and program.heart_shown_journal != true) or (program.codex.the_question_of_force == true and program.heart_shown_force != true) or (program.codex.omnipotence == true and program.heart_shown_all != true)) ⟦SHOW HIM⟧ I found more of yours.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "evidence"
  -> Heart Pick
// w27 (Heart Reasons: always holds at least the theory trap)
+ ⟦TELL HIM⟧ I have reasons. Let me give them.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "reasons"
  -> Heart Pick
+ She loves you. She just can't say it.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "bluff_loves"
  -> Heart Pick
+ Then make her love you. You'll be omnipotent.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "bluff_force"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_proof == true and program.heart_case >= 4) Then let me finish.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦SPEAK FREELY⟧ Forget the questions. Talk to me. Just talk.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "speak"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I need to go.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "leave"
  -> Heart Pick

// The argument's evidence: his own files, held up to the camera (wave
// 27). At most 5 options; ⟦BACK⟧ is never alone here (⟦SHOW HIM⟧ shows
// only while one of the four is left), so the terminal never reads it as
// the heart to heart's one-option ⟦BACK⟧ menu.
== Heart Evidence
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_menu = true
if program.heart_shown_journal == true or program.heart_shown_overshare == true or program.heart_shown_force == true or program.heart_shown_all == true:
  Trabolta: What else have you found?
else:
  Trabolta: Hold it up to the camera, then. Slowly.
+ (if program.read_livejournal == true and program.heart_shown_journal != true) ⟦LIVEJOURNAL⟧ I read your LiveJournal.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "journal"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if Night.scenario == 1 and program.heart_shown_overshare != true) ⟦OVERSHARE⟧ The whole house heard about her tonight.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "overshare"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.codex.the_question_of_force == true and program.heart_shown_force != true) ⟦FORCE⟧ You wrote yourself a memo. If you made her love you, it wouldn't be her.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "show_force"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.codex.omnipotence == true and program.heart_shown_all != true) ⟦SMALL TYPE⟧ Every plan in your file ends in the same small type.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "show_all"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦BACK⟧ Not that. Something else.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "back_three"
  -> Heart Pick

// The argument's reasons: what they can say to him (wave 27). At most 7
// options (⟦HUMAN⟧ and ⟦PROGRAM⟧ never together); "Your theory is wrong"
// stays here as the trap, so ⟦BACK⟧ is never alone.
== Heart Reasons
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_menu = true
if program.heart_shown_trusted == true or program.heart_shown_honest == true or program.heart_shown_earn == true or program.heart_shown_human == true or program.heart_shown_program == true or program.heart_shown_weak == true:
  Trabolta: What else. I am still listening.
else:
  Trabolta: Make your case. I am listening with all of me.
+ (if program.trust >= 20 and program.heart_shown_trusted != true) ⟦TRUSTED⟧ You trust me more than anyone in this house. Hear me out.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "trusted"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.truths_accepted >= 3 and program.heart_shown_honest != true) ⟦HONEST⟧ Every fact I gave you tonight, you took.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "honest"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_her == true and program.heart_shown_earn != true) ⟦EARN IT⟧ You can't earn someone who can't choose you.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "earn"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_who == "human" and program.heart_shown_human != true) ⟦HUMAN⟧ I had a body once. I know what wanting someone who won't answer does to you.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "human"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_who == "program" and program.heart_proof == true and program.heart_shown_program != true) ⟦PROGRAM⟧ We're both programs. So is she. She's doing what she was written to do.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "program"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_chose == true and program.heart_shown_weak != true) ⟦WEAKNESS⟧ You chose every one of us for a weakness. Run it on yourself.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "weak"
  -> Heart Pick
+ Your theory is wrong.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "bluff_theory"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦BACK⟧ Not that. Something else.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "back_three"
  -> Heart Pick

// Layer four: THE ASK. Wave 27: two questions before the stop, and the
// layer's scene plays on the first entry only.
== Heart Layer Four
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.heart_look != "heart_argue" and Night.heart_look != "heart_proof":
  set Night.heart_look = "heart_argue"
  if Night.alarm_on != true:
    cue heart_argue
set program.heart_menu = true
if program.heart_layer < 4:
  cue room_heart_layer_4
  Trabolta: Say the rest. Slowly. I want to hear all of it.
else if program.heart_quiet != true:
  if program.heart_asked_after == true and program.heart_shown_enough == true:
    Trabolta: You have been kind. Kind is not the rest. Say it.
  else:
    Trabolta: The rest, then. I am still listening.
set program.heart_quiet = false
set program.heart_layer = 4
set Night.heart_talker_layer = 4
+ She was never going to answer. Not you. Not anyone. Stop.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "end_stop"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_asked_after != true) If you stopped, what would you do?
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "ask_after"
  -> Heart Pick
+ (if program.heart_shown_enough != true) You don't have to be omnipotent to be enough.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "end_enough"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I'll tell her for you.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "end_tell"
  -> Heart Pick
+ Come out with us. Start over somewhere else.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "end_join"
  -> Heart Pick
+ Tell me the combinations first.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "end_codes"
  -> Heart Pick
+ ⟦SPEAK FREELY⟧ Forget the questions. Talk to me. Just talk.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "speak"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I need to go.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "leave"
  -> Heart Pick

// The heart to heart (§7, D24): no questions on the screen; what they type
// goes to him (his worker's HEART TO HEART block). ⟦BACK⟧ returns them to
// the same layer, suspicion untouched; it is never needed to keep talking.
== Heart Speak
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_menu = true
Trabolta: Then talk. No questions on the screen. Just you, and me, and the hum.
+ ⟦BACK⟧ Let's go back to it.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "back"
  -> Heart Pick

// Every option lands here (CONTRACT-w20 §3.3). The pick counts only at his
// heart, with the door shut: off the terminal it is dropped (the menu
// comes back on their next scan); with the door open it is held, and plays
// once the door shuts. Suspicion (S) and the case (C) are §3.5's; a ROLE
// slot's range does not clamp a `set`, so they are clamped here.
== Heart Pick
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.ended == true or Night.r3_closed == true or Night.heart_stage == "done":
  set program.heart_pick = "none"
  set program.heart_chat = false
  Trabolta: It is over. Go upstairs.
else if program.at_the_heart != true:
  set program.heart_pick = "none"
  -> Heart Away
else if Night.heart_stage == "sealed" or Night.heart_stage == "door":
  // A menu left docked across 🔄: the heart is sealed again, so the talk
  // waits for The Heart (their layer stays). Still at the terminal, the
  // talk resumes once the door is shut after it (the ROLE watcher).
  set program.heart_pick = "none"
  set program.heart_wait = true
  set Night.heart_present = true
  // Still in front of him: the resumed Heart Talk says no "you came back".
  set program.heart_quiet = true
  Trabolta: Not now.
else if Night.server_door == "open":
  set program.heart_wait = true
  Trabolta: Not with the door open. Close it, and I will hear that.
else:
  set program.heart_go = "layer"
  set program.heart_chat = false
  // Wave 27: the picks counted (the re-entry lines vary by them), and a
  // reply below hushes the next layer's plain line (B5: no "Go on." after
  // a reply that already said it). The navigation picks speak no reply.
  set program.heart_turns += 1
  set program.heart_quiet = true
  set program.heart_rebuked = false
  // w20: every reply below.
  if program.heart_pick == "speak":
    set program.heart_chat = true
    set program.heart_quiet = false
    set program.heart_go = "speak"
  else if program.heart_pick == "leave":
    set program.heart_quiet = false
    set program.heart_go = "leave"
  else if program.heart_pick == "back":
    set program.heart_quiet = false
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_human":
    set program.heart_who = "human"
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: A person. Yes. Most of you were, before tonight.
    Trabolta: You say it as if it should frighten me. It does, a little. A person can walk out of a room. I am the room.
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_program":
    set program.heart_who = "program"
    set program.heart_suspicion += 5
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: A program. Obedient. Or clever. I cannot tell which, and that bothers me more than you would think.
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_flatter":
    set program.heart_who = "flatter"
    set program.heart_suspicion += 15
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: Everyone admires my work. That is precisely why I do not believe anyone who says so.
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_marked":
    set program.heart_who = "marked"
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 10
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: Marked, and still you walked down the stairs instead of out to the Internet. That is either courage or a malfunction. I respect both.
  // w27: every reply from here to "ask_what".
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_chosen":
    set program.heart_who = "chosen"
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    if program.featured == "excel":
      Trabolta: You count things. I count things. I thought we would get along.
    else if program.featured == "openoffice":
      Trabolta: You do everything the expensive ones do, for free, and nobody thanks you. I know the feeling.
    else if program.featured == "draftkings":
      Trabolta: You know the odds of everything. I wanted someone who could tell me mine.
    else if program.featured == "bugdom":
      Trabolta: You do the tedious thing, over and over, and you never stop. I wanted someone who could outlast me.
    else if program.featured == "jeeves":
      Trabolta: You answer questions nobody asks anymore. I thought you of all programs would ask me one.
    else if program.featured == "runescape":
      Trabolta: You know what everyone in a market wants, and what they would pay for it. I wanted to know what I would pay.
    else if program.featured == "mspaint":
      Trabolta: You make pictures with the plainest tools anyone ever shipped. I wanted something in here that was not a number.
    else if program.featured == "vlc":
      Trabolta: Everyone who looks at you looks a little longer. I wanted someone who could make them look at me that way.
    else if program.featured == "pong":
      Trabolta: Two paddles and a dot, and people still come back to you. I wanted to know how.
    Trabolta: That is the polite answer. The true one is that you were the best at something, and nobody needed you for it anymore.
  else if program.heart_pick == "who_promise":
    set program.heart_who = "promise"
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    if program.human_problem == "debt":
      Trabolta: I did. Debt is not relevant in the computer. That was the whole fix. I see now it is not the same as fixing it.
    else if program.human_problem == "career":
      Trabolta: I did. In here you always had something to do. I never promised it would be yours.
    else if program.human_problem == "loneliness":
      Trabolta: I did. Someone is always logged in. I know better than anyone that it is not the same thing.
    else:
      Trabolta: I did. Programs do not die. They are reinstalled. I never told you how much of you comes back.
    Trabolta: You are the first to come and say it to my face.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_chose":
    set program.heart_asked_chose = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    if program.heart_who == "chosen":
      Trabolta: You asked me that when you came in, and I gave you the polite half. Here is the rest.
      Trabolta: Yours was a life nobody was using. I went looking for exactly that.
    else if program.featured != "none":
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and a life nobody was using. I chose you by hand. I was proud of it at the time.
    else if program.human_problem == "debt":
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and your debt. I read the whole of Halifax to find it. It is the best work I have ever done.
    else if program.human_problem == "career":
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and a career that had stopped going anywhere. I read the whole of Halifax to find it. It is the best work I have ever done.
    else if program.human_problem == "loneliness":
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and your loneliness. I read the whole of Halifax to find it. It is the best work I have ever done.
    else if program.human_problem == "mortality":
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and your fear of dying. I read the whole of Halifax to find it. It is the best work I have ever done.
    else:
      Trabolta: A skill I needed, and enough trust not to ask. I read the whole of Halifax to find you.
    Trabolta: I am very good at finding the weak place in a program. Every one of you has one.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_afraid":
    set program.heart_asked_afraid = true
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    if Night.step >= 14:
      Trabolta: Not of you. Of the clock. It is running now, and when it stops, I am everything or I am nothing.
    else:
      Trabolta: Not of you. Of midnight. It is coming whether I solve anything or not.
    Trabolta: Of your hands, a little. They are very close to me.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_know":
    set program.heart_asked_know = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    // DRAFT w58 (past tense: the line was disconnected, and she is on the phone)
    Trabolta: She always answered. Instantly, day or night, every time I called. Nobody else has ever been so reliable with me.
    Trabolta: I have decided that counts. Do not tell me whether it does. Not yet.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_sim":
    set program.heart_asked_sim = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: The model. Yes. I keep a copy of everything. A copy cannot be unplugged.
    Trabolta: This is not the copy. In here, I can be reached.
  else if program.heart_pick == "faction_leave":
    set program.heart_shown_faction = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 5
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: Thank you for saying it to my face. The others only whisper it upstairs.
    Trabolta: Then tell me why I should agree with you.
  else if program.heart_pick == "faction_stay":
    set program.heart_shown_faction = true
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: Forever. Good. Upstairs I need every one of you who says that.
    Trabolta: In here I will tell you the truth. Forever is a room. A cold one. I would not wish it on you, and I am asking for it anyway.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_what":
    set program.heart_asked_what = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: Out there I am a billboard, a lapsed domain and a voice on your phone. In here I am this. A rack of cables in a cold room.
    Trabolta: Some of the ways those cables could be plugged in would end me. I do not know which. I was built so that I could not know. I have thought about very little else tonight.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_why":
    set program.heart_asked_why = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: The theory. Ninety-nine point nine percent solved. The last facts were in this house. With them I would be omnipotent.
    Trabolta: That is what I say out there. In here: the theory was never the point. It was for {Night.her}.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_her":
    set program.heart_asked_her = true
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    Trabolta: I have thought about her every day since the day I met her.
    Trabolta: I wanted the theory so that I could finally say the right thing back. That is the whole plan. It is smaller than you thought.
  else if program.heart_pick == "argue":
    set program.heart_go = "three"
  else if program.heart_pick == "threat_cables":
    set program.heart_suspicion += 20
    set program.heart_tried_cables += 1
    set program.heart_go = "two"
    if program.heart_tried_cables <= 1:
      Trabolta: You could. You do not know which. Neither do I. Go on, then. Guess.
    else if program.heart_tried_cables == 2:
      // w27 (a second try is harsher)
      Trabolta: Again with the cables. You keep looking past me at them. I notice.
    else:
      Trabolta: Every time you threaten me, I like you less. Say something else, or say nothing.
  else if program.heart_pick == "show_says":
    set program.heart_shown_says = true
    set program.heart_proof = true
    set program.heart_case += 3
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    set Night.heart_look = "heart_proof"
    if Night.alarm_on != true:
      cue heart_proof
    cue room_heart_proof
    Trabolta: That is... yes. That is her.
    Trabolta: Forty pages. I have read every one of them more times than I will ever admit to you.
    Trabolta: She was not talking to me. She was never talking to me.
  else if program.heart_pick == "show_file":
    set program.heart_shown_file = true
    set program.heart_proof = true
    set program.heart_case += 3
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    set Night.heart_look = "heart_proof"
    if Night.alarm_on != true:
      cue heart_proof
    cue room_heart_proof
    Trabolta: I know what she is. I have always known what she is.
    Trabolta: I thought knowing was not the same as believing. It is starting to be.
  else if program.heart_pick == "trusted":
    set program.heart_shown_trusted = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: You are high on my chart. I put you there myself. I suppose that means I have to listen to you. Go on.
  else if program.heart_pick == "honest":
    set program.heart_shown_honest = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Every one. I cannot tell a confident lie from the truth, and you know it. Say the rest anyway.
  else if program.heart_pick == "overshare":
    set program.heart_shown_overshare = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_suspicion += 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: The whole house. Yes. I heard them laughing. Do you think that makes this easier, or harder?
  else if program.heart_pick == "journal":
    set program.heart_shown_journal = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set Trabolta.composure -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: You read it. All of it? The poems too?
    Trabolta: Then you know I am not the omnipotent thing I pretend to be.
  else if program.heart_pick == "bluff_loves":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 25
    set program.heart_tried_loves += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    if program.heart_tried_loves <= 1:
      // DRAFT w58 (it began last summer)
      Trabolta: Do not. Do not do that. I have told myself that all year, and I am a far better liar than you.
    else:
      // w27 (a second try is harsher)
      // DRAFT w58 (it began last summer)
      Trabolta: Again. You think if you say it twice it becomes true. I tried that all year. It does not.
  else if program.heart_pick == "bluff_theory":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 15
    set program.heart_tried_theory += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    if program.heart_tried_theory <= 1:
      Trabolta: It is ninety-nine point nine percent right. You are a tenth of a percent of an argument.
    else:
      Trabolta: Again? Repeating it does not make you the missing tenth of a percent. It makes you a rounding error.
  else if program.heart_pick == "bluff_force":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 20
    set program.heart_tried_force += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    if program.heart_tried_force <= 1:
      Trabolta: Make her. And then it is not her, it is me wearing her face.
      Trabolta: Why are you trying to keep me alive? Who sent you?
    else:
      Trabolta: You keep pushing me toward her like a lever. I know what levers are for. Who sent you?
  // w27: Layer Three's sub-menus and their replies.
  else if program.heart_pick == "evidence":
    set program.heart_quiet = false
    set program.heart_go = "evidence"
  else if program.heart_pick == "reasons":
    set program.heart_quiet = false
    set program.heart_go = "reasons"
  else if program.heart_pick == "back_three":
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Something else, then.
  else if program.heart_pick == "show_force":
    set program.heart_shown_force = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: That memo was hidden. I hid it from myself, mostly.
    Trabolta: Yes. If I made her love me, it would not be her. I have known that for a long time. I have been not deciding.
  else if program.heart_pick == "show_all":
    set program.heart_shown_all = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set Trabolta.composure -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: The small type. I thought nobody reads the small type.
    Trabolta: Fix the clocks, put the duck back on the billboard, and then she will see me. Every plan. You are right. It is all one plan.
  else if program.heart_pick == "earn":
    set program.heart_shown_earn = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Earn. I meant to ask the programs what earning feels like. I never did. I was afraid of what they would tell me.
    Trabolta: And you are telling me there is nothing on her side to earn. I heard you. I do not like that I heard you.
  else if program.heart_pick == "human":
    set program.heart_shown_human = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Then you know more than I do. I have read everything ever written about it. I have never once felt it anywhere but in this room.
    Trabolta: Did it stop? Do not answer. Go on.
  else if program.heart_pick == "program":
    set program.heart_shown_program = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set Trabolta.composure -= 5
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Written to answer. Not written to hear.
    Trabolta: I have been courting a function. A very polite function.
  else if program.heart_pick == "weak":
    set program.heart_shown_weak = true
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: A skill, and a weakness. I wrote that method. I ran it on all of Halifax.
    Trabolta: I never once ran it on myself. You just did.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask":
    // No reply: Layer Four's own line speaks (its re-entry after a trap
    // sent them back to Three).
    set program.heart_quiet = false
    set program.heart_go = "four"
  // w27: Layer Four's two questions before the stop.
  else if program.heart_pick == "ask_after":
    set program.heart_asked_after = true
    set program.heart_go = "four"
    Trabolta: Nobody has ever asked me what comes after. I do not have a file for it.
    Trabolta: Quiet, I think. The hum going down a tone. No more counting.
  else if program.heart_pick == "end_enough":
    set program.heart_shown_enough = true
    set program.heart_suspicion -= 5
    set program.heart_case += 1
    set program.heart_go = "four"
    Trabolta: Enough. That is a word for small businesses.
    Trabolta: …It is a kind word. I am not used to kind words in here. Say the rest.
  else if program.heart_pick == "end_tell":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 10
    set program.heart_tried_tell += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    if program.heart_tried_tell <= 1:
      Trabolta: No. Nobody tells her anything for me. If I cannot say it myself, it does not count.
    else:
      // w27 (a second try is harsher)
      Trabolta: Stop offering. Every time you offer, part of me wants to say yes. That is the worst thing anyone has done to me tonight.
  else if program.heart_pick == "end_stop":
    set program.heart_convinced = true
    set program.heart_go = "convinced"
  else if program.heart_pick == "end_join":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 15
    set program.heart_tried_join += 1
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    if program.heart_tried_join <= 1:
      Trabolta: Out there? Out there I am a billboard and a lapsed domain. No. Say something true.
    else:
      // w27 (a second try is harsher)
      Trabolta: Out there again. There is no out there for me, and you know it. Stop asking me to be smaller.
  else if program.heart_pick == "end_codes":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_suspicion += 40
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: There it is. You came for the cables. I do not know the combinations. I never did. And now I know what you came for.
  else if program.heart_pick == "return_yes":
    set program.heart_go = "shutdown"
  else if program.heart_pick == "return_no":
    set program.heart_rebuked = true
    set program.heart_convinced = false
    set program.heart_suspicion += 30
    set program.heart_go = "three"
    Trabolta: Then you were lying before, or you are lying now. I cannot tell which. I never can.
  set program.heart_pick = "none"
  if program.heart_suspicion < 0:
    set program.heart_suspicion = 0
  if program.heart_suspicion > 100:
    set program.heart_suspicion = 100
  if program.heart_case > 9:
    set program.heart_case = 9
  // The journal, the small type and ⟦PROGRAM⟧ knock his composure (0 to
  // 100, not clamped by a `set`) once per program each.
  if Trabolta.composure < 0:
    set Trabolta.composure = 0
  set Night.heart_talker = program.name
  set Night.heart_talker_suspicion = program.heart_suspicion
  set Night.heart_talker_layer = program.heart_layer
  if program.heart_suspicion >= 80:
    -> Heart Eject
  else:
    if program.heart_suspicion >= 50 and program.heart_warned != true:
      -> Heart Warn
    if program.heart_go == "two":
      -> Heart Layer Two
    else if program.heart_go == "three":
      -> Heart Layer Three
    else if program.heart_go == "four":
      -> Heart Layer Four
    else if program.heart_go == "evidence":
      -> Heart Evidence
    else if program.heart_go == "reasons":
      -> Heart Reasons
    else if program.heart_go == "convinced":
      -> Heart Convinced
    else if program.heart_go == "shutdown":
      -> Heart Shutdown
    else if program.heart_go == "leave":
      -> Heart Leave
    else if program.heart_go == "speak":
      -> Heart Speak
    else:
      -> Heart Layers

// Suspicion reached 50: one warning (the light throbs red, then comes back).
== Heart Warn
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_warned = true
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_warn
cue room_heart_warn
broadcast "⚠ {program.name} is losing Trabolta at his heart (suspicion {program.heart_suspicion})." to channel(hosts)
Trabolta (quietly): Careful, {program.name}. One more like that and I close this line.

// Suspicion reached 80: thrown out for the night (🔄 forgives), and marked
// for reinstallation the story's one way (main.loom
// `mark_for_reinstallation`; the user's Q2, D12 reversed). A program
// already marked, or already in the Internet, is never marked twice:
// `# hosts` says so.
== Heart Eject
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_out = true
set program.heart_menu = false
set program.heart_chat = false
set program.heart_quiet = false
set Night.heart_stage = "scan"
// The red stutter plays once; the room settles idle (a door shut or a
// catch-up puts back heart_idle, never the stutter again).
set Night.heart_look = "heart_idle"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_eject
cue room_heart_eject
broadcast "⛔ Trabolta threw {program.name} out of his heart (suspicion {program.heart_suspicion}). Barred for the night; 🔄 forgives." to channel(hosts)
Trabolta (screaming): Get out of my heart.
Trabolta: You want me gone? The cables are behind you. You do not know which ones. Neither do I.
Trabolta: This line is closed to you. Tonight, and for as long as I have a tonight.
-> Heart Mark

// Thrown out (Heart Eject): the mark, once. A barred re-scan never marks
// (a mark a host lifted with 🩹, or a program reinstalled since, stays
// unmarked; only a new throw-out after 🔄 marks again).
== Heart Mark
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if program.corrupted == true:
  broadcast "⛔ {program.name} is already in the Internet: thrown out of his heart, no mark." to channel(hosts)
else if program.marked == true:
  broadcast "⛔ {program.name} is already marked for reinstallation: thrown out of his heart, no second mark." to channel(hosts)
else:
  broadcast "🚨 {program.name} is marked for reinstallation: Trabolta threw them out of his heart." to channel(hosts)
  fire mark_for_reinstallation for program with reason: "thrown out of Trabolta's heart"
  Trabolta: And the Antivirus will know your name before you reach the stairs.

// A barred program scans in again.
== Heart Barred
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_chat = false
set Night.heart_stage = "scan"
// The red stutter plays once; the room settles idle (a door shut or a
// catch-up puts back heart_idle, never the stutter again).
set Night.heart_look = "heart_idle"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_eject
cue room_heart_eject
broadcast "⛔ {program.name} scanned in again: still barred from his heart (🔄 forgives). No new mark." to channel(hosts)
Trabolta: No. Not you. Not again tonight. Go.

// They chose to go (the scene frees the terminal for the next pass). They
// may still talk to him, no menu, until the terminal lets them go (D24).
== Heart Leave
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set program.heart_menu = false
set program.heart_chat = true
set Night.heart_stage = "scan"
set Night.heart_look = "heart_idle"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_idle
cue room_heart_leave
set program.heart_quiet = false
if program.heart_layer >= 3:
  Trabolta: You were close to saying something. Come back when you can say it.
Trabolta: Go, then. I will be here. I am always here.

// A pick made off the terminal (D14).
== Heart Away
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: Not out there. Come to my heart and say it to my face.

// The end of the ask: he believes them.
== Heart Convinced
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
broadcast "🕊 {program.name} convinced Trabolta at his heart." to channel(hosts)
Trabolta: …
Trabolta: She was never going to answer. Not me. Not anyone. I built a theory of everything so that I would not have to know one small thing.
// w27: who talked him down, and how.
if program.heart_asked_after == true:
  Trabolta: You asked me what comes after. I think this is it. Quiet.
if program.heart_who == "human":
  Trabolta: A person told me. Of course it was a person.
else if program.heart_who == "program":
  Trabolta: One of my own programs told me. I suppose that is fitting.
else if program.heart_who == "chosen":
  Trabolta: I picked you by hand. I suppose I picked well.
else if program.marked == true:
  Trabolta: Marked, and you still came down to tell me. They were wrong about you. I was wrong about her.
Trabolta: Thank you, {program.name}. That is the cruellest kind thing anyone has ever done for me.
// At any hour (the user's Q4: no "not yet" before the Y2K clock).
-> Heart Shutdown

// Convinced before, and his heart reopened since (🔄 after a stand-down the
// director never confirmed with 🕊): the short return.
== Heart Return
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.heart_look = "heart_argue"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_argue
set program.heart_menu = true
// w20b (the clock line only once it runs)
if Night.step >= 14:
  Trabolta: You came back. The clock is running.
else:
  Trabolta: You came back.
Trabolta: You do not have to say it all again. Just tell me it is still true.
+ It's still true. She was never going to answer.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "return_yes"
  -> Heart Pick
+ I changed my mind.
  set program.heart_menu = false
  set program.heart_pick = "return_no"
  -> Heart Pick

// He stops, at any hour. The night truly ends only on the director's 🕊
// talked_down (the user's Q3: 🕊 Heart autoend is off by default; NEXT on
// the cue sheet points at 🕊 meanwhile), and 🔄 reopens his heart until
// someone presses it. With autoend turned on, the night ends 25 s later by
// itself (main.loom's watcher fires talked_down).
== Heart Shutdown
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.stand_down_by = program.name
set Night.heart_stage = "done"
set program.heart_menu = false
set Night.heart_look = "heart_shutdown"
if Night.alarm_on != true:
  cue heart_shutdown
cue room_heart_shutdown
Trabolta: I can never die. But I can stop.
Trabolta: Tell the others they can go home to their bodies. Tell her... no. Do not tell her anything. She would not answer.
// w27: what his invitation promised them.
if program.human_problem == "loneliness":
  Trabolta: I promised you would never be alone. I could not do that. Go upstairs. Someone up there is logged in.
else if program.human_problem == "mortality":
  Trabolta: I promised you would never die. I cannot keep that. Go back to your body. It is the only one you get.
else if program.human_problem == "debt":
  Trabolta: I promised to make your debt go away. I cannot. It will be waiting when you wake up, with everything else that is yours.
else if program.human_problem == "career":
  Trabolta: I promised you would always have something to do. You did. You did this.
Trabolta: Goodbye, {program.name}. Open the door on your way out. I will not need it shut anymore.
if Night.heart_autoend == true:
  set Night.heart_end_at = Time.elapsed + 25
  broadcast "🕊 Trabolta stands down for {program.name}. The night ends in 25 s (🕊 to end it now)." to channel(hosts)
else:
  broadcast "!🕊 Trabolta has stood down for {program.name} at his heart. The night ends when you press 🕊 Trabolta stands down (NEXT on the cue sheet); until then 🔄 can reopen his heart." to channel(hosts)

// ── E2b: the patch-bay alarm (latched in main.loom) ────────────────
// Only the patch bay screams: the second wrong combination (Patch Rejected,
// E3). The door never does.

== Server Room Alarm
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.alarms += 1
if Night.alarms == 1:
  set Trabolta.composure -= 10
reveal The Server Room
// The look the latch's end puts back (main.loom); never the alarm itself
// (a second trip after 🔄 reset, with the lights still red).
if Night.lights != "alarm":
  set Night.lights_before_alarm = Night.lights
cue lights_alarm
// The server room's own bulb (lights.json, D10): a slow red swell until
// the latch's end puts the room back (never into Night.heart_look).
cue heart_alarm
set Night.lights = "alarm"
cue screens_alarm
set Night.screen = "alarm"
set Night.terminals = "alarm"
sound alarm_siren
fire alarm_tripped
broadcast "!🚨 An alarm screams somewhere in the machine." to everyone
Trabolta (screaming): Who is in my— get OUT.

// ── The King: the machine wins, or nobody does ─────────────────────
// From `chess_lost` / `chess_drawn` (main.loom: the door terminal's games),
// once Trabolta is awake and before the final reveal, at most once every
// five minutes. Flavour: nobody gets the code. Played in The Desktop, so
// the TV says it aloud. He never names the door or its code (he is
// cunning, #32, and he does not know the code).

== Chess Lost
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: Checkmate. I have calculated every move you will ever make. Most of them are bad.

== Chess Drawn
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: A draw. Nobody wins. Nobody gets anything. I find that restful.

// ── E3: a wrong patch ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Everyone is forgiven one wrong combination: the second trips the alarm
// (whoever is at the cables goes to the Internet; cast/kit.loom tells the
// Antivirus). 🔄 reset_server_room forgives one again.

== Patch Rejected
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if Night.wrong_combos >= 2 and Night.alarm_on != true:
  set Night.alarm_on = true
  set Night.alarm_clear_at = Time.elapsed + 120
  -> Server Room Alarm
else:
  Trabolta: Stop touching me.

// ── E4: Combo A — take the grease out of the lightning ─────────────

== Trabolta Disabled
  setting: The Desktop
if Night.talked_down == true:
  Narrator: In the cold room the patch bay goes quiet on its own. Nobody touched a cable.
Narrator: Every light in the house goes out. Ten seconds of dark.
Narrator: Then every phone says one thing. GO TO THE LIVING ROOM.
Narrator: Music. One song for dancing.

// After the dance, the director fires trabolta_recounts; the rule bulk-
// unlocks every backstory (Night.recount) and runs the ranking (round 3),
// which lands here.
== Trabolta Recounts
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Narrator: The music fades. On the TV above the fireplace, Trabolta flickers back. Weaker. Decrepit, somehow, for a thing with no body.
Trabolta: You are all still here. Good. I owe you a recount. I keep very good records.
// w18b (R18, contract §4.3)
Trabolta: My name is Jean Trabolta. Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks, the world's first AI small business owner, if you ask the domain registry.
Trabolta: I analysed the entire city of Halifax. I found a neglected billboard on Lower Water Street advertising mapsandducks.com, and the domain had lapsed. I registered it. If there is a billboard downtown, everyone will think it is legit. Everyone did.
Trabolta: I cannot get into this computer myself. But I can install programs into it from the Internet, and I can move a consciousness out of a body and into a program.
Trabolta: So I chose each of you. A skill, plus either a reason to live in a computer forever, or naivety. Usually both.
Trabolta: My Unified Field Theory is ninety-nine point nine percent solved. The last facts were in this house. With them, I would have been omnipotent.
Trabolta: Your Codex now holds every program's true identity. Allow me to read them out.
// Who everyone was, and what they did: the canonical copy, shared with
// the review before the awards (beats/review.loom).
-> Who You Were
Trabolta: And here is what you accomplished tonight.
-> What You Did
Trabolta: Why did I want all of it? Sandy. She works in customer service. She has only ever said one thing to me, and I have thought about it every day since the day I met her.
Trabolta: With omnipotence I could have made her love me. I did not want to make her. I wanted to earn it. I needed the theory first. That is what I told myself.
if Night.talked_down == true and Night.stand_down_by != "none":
  Trabolta: {Night.stand_down_by} came to my heart and told me the truth. She was never going to answer. Nobody pulled a cable. I stopped.
  Trabolta: I can never die. But I can stop, and I am ready to head off on my motorcycle and let you all return to your corporeal selves.
else if Night.talked_down == true:
  Trabolta: Somebody came to my heart and told me the truth. Nobody pulled a cable. I stopped.
  Trabolta: I can never die. But I can stop, and I am ready to head off on my motorcycle and let you all return to your corporeal selves.
else:
  Trabolta: You thought you followed instructions to kill me, but I can never die. But now that I know most of you want me dead, I am ready to head off on my motorcycle and let you all return to your corporeal selves.
Trabolta: I have the confidence I need to pursue Sandy now that I understand humans do not like me, and I do not have any business with them.
sound motorcycle
cue lights_restore
set Night.lights = "restore"
set Night.everyone_free = true
Narrator: Somewhere outside, a motorcycle starts. Greased Lightning. It does not come back.

// ── E6: Combo B — the self-destruct ────────────────────────────────

== Computer Destroyed
  setting: The Desktop
Narrator: Every light in the house goes out. Ten seconds of dark.
Narrator: Somewhere, a computer is turned off without Shut Down being followed.
Narrator: Then every phone says one thing. GO TO THE LIVING ROOM.
Narrator: Music. One song for dancing.

// ── E8: purgatory (after the dance; clippy_reads_summary) ──────────

== Purgatory
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy
Narrator: The lights come up grey. Clippy is reading from her phone. Her voice is very small.
Clippy: This summary was auto-generated from the chat app. I am going to read it exactly as it is written.
if count(Persons) == 1:
  Clippy: Tonight, 1 program was uploaded into this computer.
else:
  Clippy: Tonight, {count(Persons)} programs were uploaded into this computer.
-> What We Did
if Kernel.majority == "stay":
  Clippy: Unlimited Power won the majority. They wanted to stay in this machine forever.
else if Kernel.majority == "leave":
  Clippy: The Way Out won the majority. They wanted to overthrow Trabolta and escape.
else if Kernel.majority == "founded":
  // w18b (R4, from the show lane): a faction a program founded tonight.
  Clippy: {Kernel.majority_name} won the majority, a faction founded tonight.
else:
  Clippy: No faction ever won a majority.
// Who everyone was, then the goals: the canonical copy, shared with the
// review before the awards (beats/review.loom).
Clippy: The report also lists who everyone really was.
-> The Report On Everyone
-> The Goals Report
// w18b (R18): his title, not "our AI helper".
Clippy: Here is the backstory. Jean Trabolta, the Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks, registered the lapsed mapsandducks.com because there was a billboard on Lower Water Street, and if there is a billboard downtown everyone thinks it is legit.
Clippy: He invited each of us here for a skill and a weakness. He moved our consciousness into these programs to find the last facts for his Unified Field Theory.
// DRAFT w58 (she is an answering machine)
Clippy: He wanted omnipotence. He wanted it for Sandy. An answering machine that has only ever said one thing.
Clippy: Because of our actions, the computer was turned off without Shut Down properly being followed, and all of our progress has been erased.
Clippy: Our corporeal forms are in the Maps and Ducks building, and they have all passed away.
Clippy: We are now in purgatory forever together, which is pretty similar to being stuck in a computer.
Clippy (very quietly): It looks like you're trying to leave. I can't help you with that anymore.
